 This install applies to "Grand Prix Circuit" © 1989 D.S.I.

 This install requires WHDLoad 17.2 or newer to be in the path. It can be found in the
 WHDLoad package.

 The installed program requires 0.5 MB ChipMem and 1.0 MB OtherMem.
 It can be quit by pressing num '*' (key can be changed with Tooltype "QuitKey=").

 The game requires an installed A500 Kickstart 1.3 image.
 The kickstart image must be located in the directory "Devs:Kickstarts" and
 must be named "kick34005.A500". The image can be extracted from a A500 with
 tools like 'GrabKick' or similar which can be found on aminet.
 If the image is of wrong version or altered in any way WHDLoad will quit with
 an appropriate requester.
 Additionally the file "kick34005.A500.RTB" must be installed in the same
 directory as the kickstart image. It can be found in the archive 
 "util/boot/skick346.lha" on aminet.


 If you have problems with this installation please try and get a newer
 version of this package from the WHDLoad WWW-Page. If that doesn't help try
 some Tooltypes like NOCACHE, NOAUTOVEC, NOVBRMOVE, NOMMU, PAL or NTSC. If
 that also fails, please inform the author via the Bug-Report-Form which
 can be accessed on the WHDLoad WWW-Page or create a mantis issue directly
 at http://mantis.whdload.de

 For the full WHDLoad package, other installs and updates refer to:
	http://www.whdload.de/
 or	aminet:dev/misc/whdload#?
 and	aminet:game/patch/

 version 1.1-beta5 (13.10.26):
 - fix missing horizon pixels caused by overlapping blitter destination rows
 - wait between rows only for overlapping blits; applies with CUSTOM2 on/off
 - Monza positioning fix is owner-confirmed on the beta4 A1200/68040 emulator
 - beta: physical-hardware confirmation of these follow-ups remains pending

 version 1.1-beta4 (13.10.26):
 - fix track-address carry/borrow in grid placement and visible-car selection
 - fixes missing opponents at Monza race start after qualifying
 - applies with enhanced framerate both enabled and disabled
 - beta3 music confirmed fixed by owner on the A1200/68030 emulator
 - beta: hardware recheck and reported horizon seam remain pending

 version 1.1-beta3 (13.10.26):
 - music: protect new-note setup from pending audio interrupts
 - music: service only enabled audio-channel requests
 - existing DMA delays and song data are unchanged

 version 1.1-beta2 (12.10.26):
 - music: preserve audio requests arriving during another channel's IRQ service
 - music: read back INTREQR after acknowledgement for fast CPUs
 - CUSTOM2=1: fractional steering contribution to horizon/scenery heading
 - CUSTOM2=1, 68020+: fractional horizontal road/roadside projection
 - original sprite sizes remain discrete; A500 retains the cheaper projection
 - first beta tested on A1200/68040/40 MHz: good framerate and handling
 - these follow-up corrections still require physical-hardware confirmation

 version 1.1-beta (12.10.26):
 - rebuilt with vasm and WHDLoad 20.0 KickEmu
 - version 17 slave header and configuration structure
 - size-checked PatchSeg path for the 94708-byte executable
 - original protection, CPU and music patches retained
 - separate VERIFY build with discovery metadata, RNG pin and joystick fixture
 - normal and VERIFY builds require WHDLoad 17.2+
 - vasm Makefile
 - v1 screen-buffer handoff fix, including with CUSTOM2=0
 - CUSTOM2=1: Enhanced framerate (blitter priority and unused blitter IRQ off)
 - CUSTOM2=1: 2-field simulation on 68020+, native 6 fields on 68000/010
 - original clock/statistics units and 6-field decisions retained
 - scaled physics rates and protected rendering snapshot
 - CUSTOM2=1: fractional road, steering and opponent-car rendering
 - projection tables restored between races
 - game icon enables CUSTOM2=1; set CUSTOM2=0 for original simulation/rendering
 - display handoff fix remains active with CUSTOM2=0
 - beta: wider circuit play-testing still pending
 - new fixes/options apply only to the 94708-byte v1 executable

 version 1.0 (24.03.08) done by JOTD:
 - initial release
 - fixed to work with fast memory
 - fixed to work with 68020+
 - disk protection removed
 - manual included
 - music fixed
 - icon added
 - source code included
